<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salodurum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Salodurum was a Roman settlement on the River <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aare">Aare</a> in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germania">Germania</a> Superior, the origin of the Swiss town of Solothurn. It grew as a roadside village and bridge point on the route between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aventicum">Aventicum</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>. In the 4th century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> fortified it with a bell-shaped castrum, whose walls still shape the old town.</p></div>
